module ferrata_bridge_module {
  version "0.1.1"
  depends []

  method version() -> tstr description "The module's version and what was staged beside it (the commit, LEZ's, each crate's sources'\nSHA-256), as JSON."
  method deposit(request: tstr) -> tstr description "A deposit's commitment and the vault call that makes it (`deposit` or `depositETH`), and,\nwith its leaf index, the leaf, deposit id and nullifier. JSON in and out (modules/README.md)."
  method claim(request: tstr) -> tstr description "A claim of a deposit: its Merkle path in the deposit tree, the check the bridge program runs\n(`verify_claim`), its nullifier, and the program's `Claim` or `ClaimPrivately` message; given\nLEZ's state, the `ferrata` tool's claim (the program's checks, fees, accounts). JSON in and out."
  method burn(request: tstr) -> tstr description "A burn: the note (tag, memo, MAC, commitment) and the bridge program's `Burn` message, and,\nwith its index in the burn tree, the leaf, burn id and release nullifier. JSON in and out."
  method release(request: tstr) -> tstr description "A release: the burn's path in the checkpointed burn tree (its root given, or picked by the\nwallet's rule: the newest accepted root whose release delay has passed), the release guest's\ncheck (`verify_release`), its nullifier and the journal the vault verifies. JSON in and out."
  method recover(request: tstr) -> tstr description "The wallet's own deposits and burns among public ones, from its seed alone. JSON in and out."
  method status(request: tstr) -> tstr description "Where each deposit and burn stands (awaiting root, claimable, claimed; awaiting checkpoint,\nreleasable, released), from the chains' public state. JSON in and out."
  method prove_release(request: tstr) -> tstr description "A release (as `release`), then the release guest run on its input through r0vm (`program`: the\nguest's ELF), its journal checked against the native one; the tool's `release --prove`. JSON."
  method import_root(request: tstr) -> tstr description "The relayer's `ImportRoot` of a deposit root from the vault's `eth_getProof` proofs (given, or\nread at `block` through Logos Core's `eth_rpc_module` or a plain endpoint), dry-run with the\nattestation and bridge programs' own functions when the record is given. JSON."
  method registry(request: tstr) -> tstr description "The bridge program's registry as LEZ holds it (`token(cid, token)`, `config(cid)`,\n`root(cid, n)`), decoded, with a claim's schedule range and fees. JSON in and out."
  method wallet(request: tstr) -> tstr description "The mini-app's calls (`{\"method\", \"params\"}`: open, info, registry, price, deposit, scan, claim,\nburn, release), each run with the methods above over the chains' state, which a chain service\nreads and to which it signs and sends (the stand-in for Logos Core's own modules); `lez` routes the\nsession's LEZ reads and private sends through Logos Core's `lez_core`, `lez_report` lists those\ncalls; `claim` and `burn` start a job in a thread of the module and answer at once (a private one is\nproven for minutes, and a host may end the call sooner), `job` answers a job's state and, once done, its\nreply, `jobs` lists them (calls/src/jobs.rs); `seal_key` and `open_network` open a session on a Ferrata test\nnetwork's public endpoints instead (HTTPS; only the deployment the module knows; the person's recovery phrase sealed\nto the module's one-time key; for the mini-app's view only, each later call with its MAC), with `faucet`,\n`balances`, `claim`/`burn` built for approval and `confirm`, and `close` (calls/src/net.rs, seal.rs); `{\"ok\", ...}`."
  method admin(request: tstr) -> tstr description "The admin's and the freeze authority's functions: `status` (the vault's roles, registry, caps and freezes read\nthrough Logos Core's `eth_rpc_module`; LEZ's from the bridge program's states), a vault action built, checked\nwith `eth_call` from the role's account and, with `send`, handed to Logos Core's `tx_sender_module` (one\napproval in the Logos signer), or a LEZ action's message for the role's LEZ wallet. JSON in and out."
}
